msgid "meta/shortStory/ls_artefact_1"
msgstr ""
"We realized too late that each activation draws more of these beasts in."

msgid "meta/shortStory/ls_artefact_2"
msgstr ""
"We're running low on supplies, the men are exhausted, but that's not the "
"worst of it. The Mirium... it's getting to us."

msgid "meta/shortStory/ls_artefact_3"
msgstr ""
"This is it. Our last stand. The odds? Let's just say I wouldn't bet on us."

msgid "meta/shortStory/ls_artefact_4"
msgstr ""
"But if it wasn't him coming for us...where is he now? Did the echo tanks get"
" him? Or..."

msgid "meta/story/ls_artefact_1"
msgstr ""
"We repelled the first wave, but the echo tanks keep pushing. Never seen "
"anything like them—damn fierce, like something's driving them mad. Well "
"we'll figure out how to deal with these ones "
"too.{paragraph_open}{paragraph_close}The \"portal\" at the landing point is "
"dead. Engineers are working on it, but I can't just sit around waiting. Set "
"up perimeter defense. If we can't open the exit ourselves, evac team will "
"get us out. Just need to hold on.{paragraph_open}{paragraph_close}And it's "
"not coming easy. We lost half our vehicles already, now we need to replenish"
" fast. Ordered the team to crack open those "
"{violet_open}Raumfalte{violet_close}—they should have working tanks inside. "
"We realized too late that each activation draws more of these beasts in. "
"They swarm like hungry sharks to blood. But we've got no choice—we won't "
"survive without armor.{paragraph_open}{paragraph_close}Some devices were "
"empty, others had vehicles, and some had more "
"{violet_open}Raumfalte{violet_close} inside them. Like Russian nesting dolls"
" from hell.{paragraph_open}{paragraph_close}Going through Cassada's lab "
"notes. Paranoid bastard was obsessed with protecting his inventions. Keeps "
"writing: \"Stay away or the trap will snap shut!\" Well, we walked right "
"into it. But I'll figure something out—my men are getting out of here."

msgid "meta/story/ls_artefact_2"
msgstr ""
"Lost track of time in this damned space. Could be days, could be weeks. "
"We're running low on supplies, the men are exhausted, but that's not the "
"worst of it. The Mirium... it's getting to "
"us.{paragraph_open}{paragraph_close}Crew members see shadows dancing at the "
"corner of their eyes. Some of them hearing voices—strange German dialect or "
"something. Damn it, we've overstayed in this phase. Need to find a way out, "
"fast.{paragraph_open}{paragraph_close}During the rare quiet moments, I read "
"Cassada's notes. The guy hated being here as much as we do. Echo tanks drove"
" him mad—they'd swarm his lab every time he fired up the "
"{violet_open}Raumfalte{violet_close}. Eventually, he found some solution. "
"Cassada kept working, ignoring those raging beasts beneath. I'd give "
"anything to know what he figured out.{paragraph_open}{paragraph_close}Now my"
" men are mumbling about \"Cassada calling them deeper\", saying he's coming "
"for us.{paragraph_open}{paragraph_close}Clock's ticking. A little longer and"
" we'll all lose our minds in here. But I'll be damned if we go quietly. "
"We're doing it in a blaze of glory, dragging these creatures down with us."

msgid "meta/story/ls_artefact_3"
msgstr ""
"The sky darkened in an instant. First came the shadow, then it swallowed up "
"the entire sky. And then we saw it—a colossal airship materializing from the"
" darkness.{paragraph_open}{paragraph_close}My men were terrified at first. "
"They've been whispering about Cassada for days, and now they're convinced "
"he's here for revenge. We raided his lab, stole his precious devices, and "
"now this monstrosity appears.{paragraph_open}{paragraph_close}Men are "
"running on pure adrenaline—haven't slept in what feels like weeks. But you "
"should see their faces... Even now, as that monster casts its shadow over "
"us, not one of them has abandoned their "
"post.{paragraph_open}{paragraph_close}This is it. Our last stand. The odds? "
"Let's just say I wouldn't bet on us. But we'll give that bastard Cassada a "
"fight he'll remember! Roll out!"

msgid "meta/story/ls_artefact_4"
msgstr ""
"That monstrosity in the sky wasn't Cassada after all—it was "
"ours.{paragraph_open}{paragraph_close}Extraction team said they fought "
"interference for days trying to reach us. Guess that was Cassada's trap—not "
"the ship, but the signal blockade. Clever "
"bastard.{paragraph_open}{paragraph_close}But if it wasn't him coming for "
"us...where is he now? Did the echo tanks got him? Or... I don't even want to"
" think about that.{paragraph_open}{paragraph_close}Command's hauling all "
"those {violet_open}Raumfalte{violet_close} devices to their vaults. More "
"experiments, more secrets. Sometimes I wonder if we're really in control of "
"this Mirium stuff, or if it's playing us all for fools. Maybe Merkulov was "
"right with his bomb?{paragraph_open}{paragraph_close}To hell with "
"philosophy. Right now I just need to sleep. Finally, get some real sleep."

